{"total_count":9,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12120","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12120/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12120/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12120/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12120","id":3020244366,"node_id":"I_kwDOAI0trM60BUWO","number":12120,"title":"[scroll-animations-1] it is not clear when to update stale timelines","user":{"login":"graouts","id":49648,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49648?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts","html_url":"https://github.com/graouts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graouts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1561535155,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNTYxNTM1MTU1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/scroll-animations-1","name":"scroll-animations-1","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"Current Work","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2025-04-25T14:34:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T07:32:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The [HTML Processing Model: Event loop section of the Scroll-driven Animations spec](https://drafts.csswg.org/scroll-animations-1/#event-loop) discusses how scroll and view timelines may become stale in the process of updating the rendering since timeline sources or subjects may change bounds during that process.\n\nHowever, the spec does not reference the HTML spec with hard links and rather references sections which are by now outdated. For instance (at the time of writing this issue), the step to update animations and send events is step 11 and the current spec references step 10. As such it is not clear exactly when in the process of updating the page rendering stale timelines should be updated. Using informative notes, it appears it is after resize observers have been evaluated and styles have been recalculated and layout updated.\n\nWe should probably update the HTML spec itself to add a step that clearly references the process of updating stale timelines.\n\nHere are related spec issues and spec change:\n\n- [[scroll-animations] Behavior of scroll-linked animations in the first frame](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5261)\n- [[scroll-animations-1] Handling changed size/position in current frame](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/8694)\n- [additional spec change](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/8704)\n\nCc @flackr who made the spec change as well as @kevers-google and @andruud who reviewed it.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12120/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12120/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14344","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14344/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14344/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14344/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14344","id":5185938631,"node_id":"I_kwDOAI0trM8AAAABNRskxw","number":14344,"title":"[css-values-5] Add `calc-range()`, inverse of `progress()`?","user":{"login":"tabatkins","id":682840,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4Mjg0MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins","html_url":"https://github.com/tabatkins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":971551685,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NzE1NTE2ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/css-values-5","name":"css-values-5","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-08-18T20:20:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T19:25:50Z","closed_at":"2026-09-04T19:25:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The `progress()` function takes a value, and a min/max, and returns a number indicating what progress the \"value\" represents between the min/max. (Or before/after the min/max, if unclamped.) That is, `progress(50px, 0px, 200px)` return `0.25`.\n\nThe inverse operation can also be useful - given a progress value, and a min/max representing the 0/1 progress value, return the corresponding value. \n\nThis actually *already exists* in the spec, just accidentally: `random(fixed 0.25, 0px, 200px)` will return `50px`. It's pretty weird to (mis)use `random()` for this, though!\n\nWould it be worth adding the functionality directly to the spec? This isn't *just* a trivial linear transform, as `random()` also has useful *step* behavior that is either complicated or impossible to reproduce manually (I haven't worked at it yet to tell for sure whether you can actually do it with full fidelity, given the end-clamping behavior). That is, `calc-range(N, 0px, 200px, 50px)` would only return 5 possible values - 0px, 50px, 100px, 150px, and 200px, each taking 20% of the 0-1 argument range.\n\n----------\n\nLittle side feature discussion - the current `random()` behavior for steps is pretty specialized to the \"clamped to 0-1\" requirement that random() imposes. If you allowed values <0 or >1, it's no longer perfectly symmetrical, as the first/last values would be overrepresented; in the previous example, `200px` would be returned for the range `[.8, 1)`, and *also* for `[1, 1.2)`.\n\nPossibly, for both this function and for random(), we could allow optionally specifying [one of the `jump-*` keywords from `steps()`](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-easing-2/#valdef-step-position-jump-start), defaulting to `jump-none` when unspecified.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14344/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11970","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11970/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11970/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11970/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11970","id":2936694387,"node_id":"I_kwDOAI0trM6vCmZz","number":11970,"title":"[css-easing] Allow `steps()` to accept an easing function as the `<step-position>`","user":{"login":"bramus","id":213073,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzA3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213073?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus","html_url":"https://github.com/bramus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bramus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":469426704,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0Njk0MjY3MDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Needs%20Edits","name":"Needs Edits","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":534594975,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1MzQ1OTQ5NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/css-easing-2","name":"css-easing-2","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"Current Work","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2025-03-20T21:30:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T21:11:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Recently Vasilis [asked](https://front-end.social/@vasilis@social.vasilis.nl/114174299342016142):\n\n> Dearest CSS working group, I want to be able to define a transition between the steps in an animation-timing-function. Can you please fix this?\n\nThey needed this create the seconds hand of this clock which uses an `ease` between every second it ticks: https://vasilis.nl/clocks/station-clock/01/\n\nAs a workaround I [pointed](https://front-end.social/@bramus/114174411047664584) them to creating a bunch of keyframes and setting the `animation-timing-function` per keyframe, which they did, resulting in _a lot_ of code.:\n\n```css\n/* \nVery annoying, but this is, for now, the only way to \ntransition between steps() in a keyframe animation.\nHad to write out every percentage. \n*/\n@keyframes ticking {\n\t0% {\n\t\trotate: 0deg;\n\t\tanimation-timing-function: ease;\n\t}\n\t1.66666666% {\n\t\trotate: 6deg;\n\t\tanimation-timing-function: ease;\n\t}\n\t3.33333333% {\n\t\trotate: 12deg;\n\t\tanimation-timing-function: ease;\n\t}\n\t…\n\t98.33333333% {\n\t\trotate: 354deg;\n\t\tanimation-timing-function: ease;\n\t}\n\t100% {\n\t\trotate: 360deg;\n\t\tanimation-timing-function: ease;\n\t}\n}\n.seconds {\n  animation: ticking 58s linear;\n}\n```\n\n_(Not sure why they chose `58s`, though)_\n\nIf [`steps()`](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-easing-2/#step-easing-function) were to accept another easing function as the `<step-position>`, the code could be simplified to the following:\n\n```css\n@keyframes ticking {\n  to {\n    rotate: 360deg;\n  }\n}\n\n.seconds {\n  animation: ticking 60s steps(60, ease);\n}\n```\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11970/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11970/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5321","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5321/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5321/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5321/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5321","id":656868286,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU2NTY4NjgyODY=","number":5321,"title":"[scroll-animations] TAG feedback: interaction with prefers reduced motion","user":{"login":"majido","id":944639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0NDYzOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/944639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido","html_url":"https://github.com/majido","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/majido/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":511772377,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1MTE3NzIzNzc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/a11y-tracker","name":"a11y-tracker","color":"ea7472","default":false,"description":"Group bringing to attention of a11y, or tracked by the a11y Group but not needing response.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1561535155,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNTYxNTM1MTU1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/scroll-animations-1","name":"scroll-animations-1","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"Current Work","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":17,"created_at":"2020-07-14T20:09:38Z","updated_at":"2022-11-18T20:43:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Here is a question/feedback from TAG. The original is [here](https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/521#issuecomment-657984261) but I am creating this issue to track this in CSSWG as well.\r\n\r\n> Given that one of the use cases this API is explicitly designed to enable is parallax scroll effects, which is a known trigger for vestibular disorders, it might be worth considering how this feature integrates with prefers-reduced-motion.\r\n\r\n> For example, should animations expressed using this API be disabled by default if `prefers-reduced-motion` would match? And if so, could we design a way to allow animations to express that they are safe to be shown for users who prefer reduced motion?\r\n\r\n> I think it might even be worth opening a broader discussion on what the default behaviour for prefers-reduced-motion should be for all web APIs which allow animation, but I think the question is especially critical for this API given it's more likely than average to cause harm to users.\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/5321/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12919","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12919/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12919/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12919/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12919","id":3496630650,"node_id":"I_kwDOAI0trM7Qall6","number":12919,"title":"[css-overscroll] overscroll-behavior should not prevent visual viewport \"panning\"","user":{"login":"vmpstr","id":1906955,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MDY5NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1906955?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr","html_url":"https://github.com/vmpstr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vmpstr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":469426704,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0Njk0MjY3MDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Needs%20Edits","name":"Needs Edits","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":665433501,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NjU0MzM1MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Needs%20Testcase%20(WPT)","name":"Needs Testcase (WPT)","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":892569012,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTI1NjkwMTI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/css-overscroll-1","name":"css-overscroll-1","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2025-10-08T19:28:18Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T01:37:49Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"If I have a scroller with [overscroll-behavior: contain](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overscroll/#overscroll-behavior-properties), and I pinch-zoom in (on my macbook), then while my mouse cursor is over this contained scroller, I am unable to pan around the [visual viewport](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view-1/#visualViewport).\n\nThis is probably a correct behavior per spec, since the visual viewport refers to scrolling and overscroll-behavior contains the scrolling. This is also reproducible in Safari, Firefox, and Chrome. However, as a user, I find this to be not what I would expect.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12919/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12919/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11742","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11742/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11742/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11742/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11742","id":2861983625,"node_id":"I_kwDOAI0trM6qlmeJ","number":11742,"title":"[css-values-5] Maybe min, max and step should not be part of the random-caching-key","user":{"login":"smfr","id":20968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr","html_url":"https://github.com/smfr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smfr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":395785969,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzOTU3ODU5Njk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Closed%20Accepted%20by%20CSSWG%20Resolution","name":"Closed Accepted by CSSWG Resolution","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Changes backed by a CSSWG resolution.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":971551685,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NzE1NTE2ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/css-values-5","name":"css-values-5","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":46,"created_at":"2025-02-19T01:16:58Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T20:58:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Currently, CSS Values 5 says that the [min, max and step are part of the `random-caching-key`](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-values-5/#random-caching).\n\nHowever, this prevents some possibly useful techniques where an element shares the same random value, but with different min, max and step with another property on the same element, or with another element. \n\nConceptually, I would expect that the underlying 0-1 random number is sampled based only on the `dashed-ident` or `per-element` keyword, and then min, max and step are just math applied to that underlying value.\n\nConsider\n```\n        .box {\n            background-color: blue;\n            height: random(per-element, 50px, 100px);\n            width: random(per-element, 100px, 200px);\n        }\n```\n\nI want this box to have a random size, but always a 2/1 aspect ratio. With the current spec, width and height get their own random values.\n\nAnother example might be that you have two elements that want a width based on a single random value, but they quantize that value in different ways.\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11742/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7317","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7317/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7317/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7317/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7317","id":1250029803,"node_id":"I_kwDOAI0trM5KgfDr","number":7317,"title":"[cssom-view] Rename Element.isVisible to Element.isHidden?","user":{"login":"chrishtr","id":3453258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NTMyNTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3453258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr","html_url":"https://github.com/chrishtr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrishtr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":469426704,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0Njk0MjY3MDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Needs%20Edits","name":"Needs Edits","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":24,"created_at":"2022-05-26T20:28:29Z","updated_at":"2023-10-18T22:38:00Z","closed_at":"2022-06-29T21:02:11Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In Issue #6850 we decided to add [`isVisible`](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#dom-element-isvisible). Should we rename it to `isHidden` and flip the return value?\r\n\r\nThe only difference I can see is that it flips what is considered a \"positive\" result, and therefore maybe developers would be less likely to misinterpret the results. i.e. developers might interpret `isVisible` as a stronger assertion from the browser than \"not `isHidden`\". Since `isVisible` does not actually mean \"guaranteed to be visible right now to the user\", maybe `isHidden` is better?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7317/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7317/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1680","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1680/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1680/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1680/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1680","id":247445979,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNDc0NDU5Nzk=","number":1680,"title":"[css-timing] Names for keyword arguments to steps timing function","user":{"login":"ewilligers","id":929206,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTIwNg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/929206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers","html_url":"https://github.com/ewilligers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewilligers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":534594911,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1MzQ1OTQ5MTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/css-easing-1","name":"css-easing-1","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":11,"created_at":"2017-08-02T16:18:23Z","updated_at":"2018-09-26T01:17:37Z","closed_at":"2018-09-25T08:22:31Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The decision in today's Paris F2F is that the examples\r\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1301#issuecomment-310571203\r\nwill be\r\nsteps(3, ?), start(3, ?)\r\nsteps(4, ?), steps(2, ?)\r\nwhere the keywords are TBD.\r\n\r\nstart and end will continue to be supported, but there is the option of aliasing them to new keywords.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1680/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1680/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/401","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/401/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/401/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/401/events","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/401","id":170788681,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzA3ODg2ODE=","number":401,"title":"[css-flexbox] Absolute Positioned Elements in Flex Containers Removes Common Layout Patterns","user":{"login":"jlukic","id":23123,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMTIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23123?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic","html_url":"https://github.com/jlukic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlukic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":381889006,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzODE4ODkwMDY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/css-flexbox-1","name":"css-flexbox-1","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"Current Work","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":395791591,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzOTU3OTE1OTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Commenter%20Timed%20Out%20(Assumed%20Satisfied)","name":"Commenter Timed Out (Assumed Satisfied)","color":"99ff99","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":435840171,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MzU4NDAxNzE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Closed%20Rejected%20as%20Wontfix%20by%20CSSWG%20Resolution","name":"Closed Rejected as Wontfix by CSSWG Resolution","color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":856066418,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NTYwNjY0MTg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/labels/Tracked%20in%20DoC","name":"Tracked in DoC","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/milestones/1","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/milestone/1","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/milestones/1/labels","id":3229777,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMzIyOTc3Nw==","number":1,"title":"css-flexbox-1 2017-10-19+","description":"Issues against https://www.w3.org/TR/2017/CR-css-flexbox-1-20171019/\r\nFixed in https://www.w3.org/TR/2018/CR-css-flexbox-1-20181119/","creator":{"login":"fantasai","id":725717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTcxNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/725717?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai","html_url":"https://github.com/fantasai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fantasai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":37,"state":"closed","created_at":"2018-03-29T21:03:41Z","updated_at":"2019-01-23T00:06:16Z","due_on":"2018-11-19T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2018-03-29T21:05:38Z"},"comments":14,"created_at":"2016-08-12T02:43:01Z","updated_at":"2018-03-29T21:04:29Z","closed_at":"2017-03-22T17:13:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-flexbox/#abspos-items\n\nCurrently Flexbox spec does not allow absolutely positioned elements inside a flex container to preserve their calculated position when using `top: auto;` or `left:auto;` (its initial value). \n\nHere's an example of this behavior in both `flex` and normal containers.\nhttps://jsfiddle.net/91tn25zn/\n\nOutside of flex containers using `auto` positioning values behaves this way, so this is _new_ behavior added in flex. \n\nThis behavior inside flex containers removed a very important method for positioning elements in CSS, allowing elements to exist outside of page flow but preserve their calculated positions. For example this breaks all [vertical dividers in Semantic UI](http://semantic-ui.com/elements/divider.html#vertical-divider) which represents a common design pattern of adding elements which do not participate in layout, but are used for styling based on their rendered position.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/401/reactions","total_count":25,"+1":25,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/401/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}